    "stop_reason": "success",
    "result_text": "All tests pass (`BUILD SUCCESS`, 2/2, including `coreRejectsDuplicateTelephone` expecting 409 and `functionalityAllowsDistinctTelephone`).\n\n## What I did\n\nThe `POST /api/owners` pipeline normalizes the telephone (strip non-digits \u2192 10 digits) but had no uniqueness check. I added a step right after normalization:\n\n- **`RejectDuplicateTelephone`** (new function) \u2014 after `NormalizeOwnerTelephone`, before `BuildOwner`. It compares the request's normalized telephone against the normalized telephone of every existing owner via the repository's existing `findAll()`, throwing `DuplicateTelephoneException` on a collision. Using `findAll()` kept all three repository implementations untouched.\n- **`DuplicateTelephoneException`** \u2014 a checked exception (so it surfaces in `throws`, per the escalation convention).\n- **`DuplicateTelephoneHandler`** + its escalation YAML (`officefloor/escalation/...DuplicateTelephoneException.yml`) \u2014 responds **409 Conflict**.\n- Wired `owners.POST.yml`: `normalizeTelephone \u2192 rejectDuplicateTelephone \u2192 build`.\n\nThe check runs before the transactional `build`/`save` steps, comparing normalized-to-normalized so it catches duplicates regardless of formatting in stored data.",
